{"id": "EUVD-2023-60712", "enisaUuid": "e908650c-10c8-3fad-97d9-006424e3e977", "description": "Frappe before 14.59.0 and 15.x before 15.5.0 contains a sandbox flaw where the frappe.flags.in_safe_exec global flag can become False during Server Script execution when one server script triggers another. Authenticated high-privileged users can craft a Server Script that triggers other server scripts, such as by saving a document, so the remaining code runs without safe execution protections.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T22:21:38", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T14:03:30", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:H/UI:N/VC:N/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/frappe/frappe/security/advisories/GHSA-v3vh-7qx4-f582", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/frappe-before-14.59.0-safe-execution-flag-bypass-in-server-scripts"], "aliases": ["CVE-2023-54406", "GHSA-fg2g-fx2h-8fqw"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.32, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "331f01d3-7520-3a27-842e-697c94018d1e", "product": {"name": "frappe", "vendor": {"name": "Elated-Themes"}}, "product_version": "0 <14.59.0"}, {"id": "e2ac944f-9d4f-3e68-9e98-1c6701e133bc", "product": {"name": "frappe", "vendor": {"name": "Elated-Themes"}}, "product_version": "15.0.0 <15.5.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "257d1fb4-6a7e-3988-82af-7b2cd12a6e40", "vendor": {"name": "frappe"}}], "isExploited": false}